# Shell scripts must stay LF: core.autocrlf would otherwise smudge them to CRLF on
# Windows checkouts, which breaks the shebang under bash on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Markdown must stay LF for the same reason, one layer up, and it is load-bearing rather than
# cosmetic. The synthetic notes are Markdown, `app.py` reads an upload as raw bytes, and every
# other reader goes through `Path.read_text`, which collapses CRLF before anything sees it. So a
# note smudged to CRLF on checkout reached the pipeline as a *different string* than the one the
# cassettes were recorded against and the ground truth describes: cassette miss, live API call,
# and on a keyless clone a failure. Without this line `verify.sh ALL --offline` failed 13 tests on
# Windows and passed on Linux — the worst shape a bug can take on a two-machine project.
#
# `read_upload` normalises newlines too. This fixes the checkout; that fixes the upload, which is
# the half a judge can still break by re-saving a downloaded note in an editor.
*.md text eol=lf
